Do not free the OSD overlay's CMA memory: the display is reading it

The vendor's OSD driver releases the overlay's CMA memory a minute
after start-up, on the assumption that nothing is using the overlay by
then. On this box the overlay IS the display: the DRM's primary plane
scans it, and the text console draws into it - the DRM debugfs shows
the plane enabled, with the console's own framebuffer on it, at the
overlay's address.

So the release pulls the memory out from under the display, the HDMI
transmitter keeps scanning it, and the machine dies - a hard reset,
with no message, because the fault is in the DMA path. It looks like
a spontaneous reboot every minute or so.

The memory is returned when the system reboots, and 8 MB out of the
688 MB of CMA this kernel reserves is not worth a display that dies
every minute.
diff --git a/drivers/amlogic/media/osd/osd_fb.c b/drivers/amlogic/media/osd/osd_fb.c
--- a/drivers/amlogic/media/osd/osd_fb.c
+++ b/drivers/amlogic/media/osd/osd_fb.c
@@ -5541,8 +5541,27 @@
 	if (osd_meson_dev.has_viu2)
 		vout2_register_client(&osd_notifier_nb2);
 #endif
+	/*
+	 * Do NOT free the OSD overlay's CMA memory.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor's driver releases it a minute after start-up, on the
+	 * assumption that nothing is using the overlay by then. On this
+	 * box the overlay IS the display: the DRM's primary plane scans
+	 * it, and the text console draws into it - the DRM debugfs shows
+	 * the plane enabled, with the console's own framebuffer on it, at
+	 * the overlay's address.
+	 *
+	 * So the release pulls the memory out from under the display,
+	 * the HDMI transmitter keeps scanning it, and the machine dies -
+	 * a hard reset, with no message, because the fault is in the DMA
+	 * path. It looks like a spontaneous reboot every minute or so.
+	 *
+	 * The memory is returned when the system reboots, and 8 MB out of
+	 * the 688 MB of CMA this kernel reserves is not worth a display
+	 * that dies every minute.
+	 */
 	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&osd_dwork, mem_free_work);
-	schedule_delayed_work(&osd_dwork, msecs_to_jiffies(60 * 1000));
+	/* schedule_delayed_work(&osd_dwork, msecs_to_jiffies(60 * 1000)); */
 
 	osd_log_info("osd probe OK\n");
 	return 0;
